From 9c220280e0ce53efb670e16454bfaa0891f598e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mamam Kasir Dev <dev@mamamayam.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:58:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Riwayat Transaksi & Detail (transaction history +
 cancel flow)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires up the dashboard's 'Riwayat' quick action, previously a stub.
Transactions already persisted to DB from checkout — this reads them back.

Scope decided from PRD, not the React reference app (reference's
recycle-bin/hard-delete/bulk-select pattern explicitly rejected):
- 'Batalkan Transaksi' (cancel, not delete) — canceled stays in history
  shown red/struck-through, excluded from omzet in the payment breakdown,
  no refund transaction created, cannot cancel/edit again once canceled
- Transaction hard-delete is NOT implemented — PRD explicitly leaves
  deletion permission/retention UNSPECIFIED
- Cancel has no role-gating yet (Auth/Permissions module doesn't exist);
  open to anyone for now, role restrictions land once Auth is built

DB (v3): added transactions.canceled_at / cancel_reason columns.

New history feature module:
- Domain: HistoryDateFilter (Hari Ini/Kemarin/Hari Sebelumnya/Custom per
  PRD's explicit list, plus Bulan Ini/Semua as practical additions under
  PRD's 'plus relevant filters' allowance), HistorySortKey,
  PaymentMethodBreakdown
- Application: HistoryRepository (reads transactions+items back into
  domain models, handles cancel — no delete method exists at all),
  HistoryController/HistoryState with search + date/order-type/
  payment-method filtering, sort, and a payment-method revenue breakdown
  computed independently of the payment-method filter itself
- Presentation: HistoryScreen (search, date filter tabs, order-type
  filter row, payment breakdown card, sortable list), TransactionCard
  (canceled transactions shown red/struck-through), TransactionDetailScreen
  (full itemized detail + Batalkan action with reason capture), plus
  DateFilterTabs/PaymentBreakdownCard/SortSheet widgets

Same Transaction/sqflite_common naming clash as pos_repository.dart
applies here too — history_repository.dart imports our Transaction model
as 'txn' from the start, so no follow-up fix needed for this one.
